#![allow(clippy::excessive_precision)]
//! Golden-parity test for `stamp_volcanoes_provinces` (PARITY_TESTING.md).
//! Reference HTML `stampVolcanoesProvinces`/`placeProvinceVolcanoes`/
//! `placeSizedVolcano` (lines 3487-3556). Unlike `build_orogeny_field`,
//! none of these JS functions are pure -- they read `GW`/`GH`/`state`/
//! `field`/`boundaryMask`/etc. as globals, so a Node `vm` sandbox's normal
//! `let`/`const`-doesn't-attach-to-context limitation (see the orogeny
//! golden test's own doc comment) would make them unreachable entirely.
//!
//! Unblocked by a harness upgrade: rewriting top-level (zero-indent) `let`/
//! `const` to `var` before `vm` execution attaches those bindings to the
//! sandbox context object, which in turn made it possible to set a small
//! GW/GH, call `allocate()`, and drive the actual unmodified `generate()`
//! pipeline end to end -- then monkey-patch `stampVolcanoesProvinces`
//! itself to snapshot its real inputs (boundaryMask/stressField/plateId/
//! plates/field, all genuinely produced by `generate()`'s own earlier
//! stages, not hand-constructed) and its real effect on `field`/
//! `volcanicField`. Captured at seed 42, 20x14, mapWidthKm
//! 800, volc.provinces=true, volc.count=20.

